IMPORT prelude

-- Hydrogen Cyanide (Fumigation) Act 1947 (Singapore) -- the whole Act as it bears on a fumigator or a person who has fumigation
-- done: the reach of the regulation-making power and the open-air exclusion (s 2(1), (3)), the offence and fine for breaking the
-- regulations (s 2(4)), the duty to notify the Minister of an accident causing death or injury (s 3), offences against a formal
-- investigation (s 4(e)), the Coroner's duty to adjourn (s 5), and extension to other gases (s 6).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/HCFA1947.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the deposit's metadata calls it the
-- current version as at 1 October 2026. The only amendment annotated in the body is [40/2019], against s 4.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0090 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl): Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is six sections long, so nearly all of it is encoded. Not encoded: the list of subjects the regulations may
-- cover (s 2(2)) beyond a comment, the annulment procedure for regulations (s 2(5)), the conduct of an inquiry and a formal
-- investigation (s 4(a) to (d), (f)) beyond witness expenses and the report, and s 5(2), (4). The regulations themselves were not
-- retrieved, so what they require of a fumigator is unknown here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Hydrogen Cyanide (Fumigation) Act 1947`

DECLARE Gas IS ONE OF
    `hydrogen cyanide`
    `another substance`

DECLARE Fumigation HAS
    `the gas` IS A Gas
    `a section 6 order applies the Act to the substance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `carried out in the open air` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `6 -- other gases`

-- s 6: "The Minister may by order apply the provisions of this Act or such of those provisions as may be specified in the order to
-- fumigation with any substance other than hydrogen cyanide in like manner as they apply to fumigation with hydrogen cyanide".
-- Naive: an order that applies only some provisions is modelled as applying the whole Act.
GIVEN `the fumigation` IS A Fumigation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act reaches the fumigation` IF
    CONSIDER `the fumigation`'s `the gas`
    WHEN `hydrogen cyanide` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another substance` THEN `the fumigation`'s `a section 6 order applies the Act to the substance`

§§ `2 -- regulations, the open-air exclusion, and the fine`

-- s 2(1): "With a view to protecting persons from danger in connection with the fumigation of premises and articles (including any
-- ship or vehicle) with hydrogen cyanide, the Minister may make regulations with respect to such fumigation."
-- (2): they may regulate how the gas is generated, require trained supervision and a specified number of persons, require a
-- licence, regulate licences and their fees, regulate disposal of residues, and impose temporary restrictions and post-fumigation
-- tests.
-- (3): "Regulations made under this section shall not apply to any such fumigation carried out in the open air."
GIVEN `the fumigation` IS A Fumigation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the regulations apply to the fumigation` IF
    `the Act reaches the fumigation` `the fumigation` AND (NOT `the fumigation`'s `carried out in the open air`)

-- (4): "If any person contravenes any regulations made under this section, he shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- conviction in respect of each offence to a fine not exceeding $500." No imprisonment.
GIVEN `the fumigation` IS A Fumigation, `did what the regulations forbid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `contravening the regulations is an offence` IF
    `the regulations apply to the fumigation` `the fumigation` AND `did what the regulations forbid`

GIVEN `number of contraventions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum total fine for contravening the regulations` IS
    500 * `number of contraventions`

§§ `3 -- notice of accidents`

-- s 3(1): "Whenever any accident which occasions loss of human life or personal injury occurs as the result of the fumigation of
-- any premises or article, the person by whom, or by whose agent, the fumigation was carried out shall forthwith send or cause to be
-- sent to the Minister notice of the accident and of the loss of human life or personal injury."
-- (2): contravention is an offence, fine not exceeding $200.
-- s 3 has no open-air exclusion: s 2(3) limits only the regulations. The words of s 3 do not repeat "with hydrogen cyanide"; reading
-- s 3 as confined to fumigations the Act reaches (s 6) is an INFERENCE from the long title and s 6, and it is the reading encoded.
DECLARE Harm IS ONE OF
    `loss of human life`
    `personal injury`
    `damage to property only`
    `no harm`

DECLARE Relation IS ONE OF
    `carried out the fumigation personally`
    `the fumigation was carried out by its agent`
    `owns the premises fumigated by an independent fumigator`
    `a bystander`

GIVEN `the fumigation` IS A Fumigation, `the harm` IS A Harm
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `notice of the accident is required` IF
    `the Act reaches the fumigation` `the fumigation`
    AND CONSIDER `the harm`
        WHEN `loss of human life` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `personal injury` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Who must send it. Naive: an owner who engages a fumigator is not treated as the fumigator's principal; whether the fumigator is
-- its "agent" is a question the text leaves open.
GIVEN `the relation` IS A Relation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `bears the duty to notify` IF
    CONSIDER `the relation`
    WHEN `carried out the fumigation personally` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the fumigation was carried out by its agent` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the fumigation` IS A Fumigation, `the harm` IS A Harm, `the relation` IS A Relation, `sent notice forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to notify is an offence` IF
        `notice of the accident is required` `the fumigation` `the harm`
    AND `bears the duty to notify` `the relation`
    AND (NOT `sent notice forthwith`)

`the maximum fine for failing to notify` MEANS 200

§§ `4 -- inquiry and formal investigation`

-- s 4: the Minister "may direct an inquiry" into an accident of which notice is required, and may order a formal investigation.
-- (d): witnesses get "such expenses as would be allowed to witnesses attending before the General Division of the High Court";
-- disputes go to the Registrar of the Supreme Court.
-- (e): "if any person without reasonable excuse (proof of which shall lie on him) fails, after having had the expenses (if any) to
-- which he is entitled tendered to him, to comply with any summons or requisition of the court ..., or prevents or impedes the court
-- in the execution of its duty, he shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $100, or,
-- in the case of a failure to comply with a requisition for furnishing any return or producing any document, to a fine not exceeding
-- $100 for every day on which the failure occurs or continues".
-- (f): the report goes to the Minister, who "shall cause every report so made to him to be made public".
-- Naive: the expenses condition is read as attaching to failing to comply, not to impeding.
DECLARE Default IS ONE OF
    `ignoring a summons to attend`
    `failing to furnish a return`
    `failing to produce a document`
    `impeding the court`

GIVEN `the default` IS A Default, `proved a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `entitled to expenses` IS A BOOLEAN, `expenses tendered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the default is an offence` IF
        (NOT `proved a reasonable excuse`)
    AND CONSIDER `the default`
        WHEN `impeding the court` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE (NOT `entitled to expenses`) OR `expenses tendered`

GIVEN `the default` IS A Default, `days the failure continues` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine for the default` IS
    CONSIDER `the default`
    WHEN `failing to furnish a return` THEN 100 * `days the failure continues`
    WHEN `failing to produce a document` THEN 100 * `days the failure continues`
    OTHERWISE 100

§§ `5 -- Coroner's inquiry`

-- s 5(1): where a Coroner holds an inquiry on a death that may have been caused by an accident of which notice is required, "the
-- Coroner shall adjourn the inquiry unless some person on behalf of the Minister is present to watch the proceedings except that, if
-- the accident has not occasioned the death of more than one person, and the Coroner has sent to the Minister notice of the time and
-- place of holding the inquiry not less than 48 hours before the time of holding it, it shall not be imperative on him to adjourn".
GIVEN `the Minister is represented` IS A BOOLEAN, `deaths in the accident` IS A NUMBER, `hours of notice to the Minister` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Coroner must adjourn` IF
        (NOT `the Minister is represented`)
    AND (NOT (`deaths in the accident` AT MOST 1 AND `hours of notice to the Minister` AT LEAST 48))

-- (3): "The Coroner shall, at least 4 days before holding the adjourned inquiry, send to the Minister notice in writing".
GIVEN `days of notice before the adjourned inquiry` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `notice of the adjourned inquiry is in time` IF
    `days of notice before the adjourned inquiry` AT LEAST 4

-- (5): where evidence is given "of any neglect having caused or contributed to an accident, the Coroner shall, if no person employed
-- on behalf of the Minister is present at the inquiry, send to the Minister notice in writing of the neglect."
GIVEN `evidence of neglect` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister is represented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Coroner must notify the Minister of neglect` IF
    `evidence of neglect` AND (NOT `the Minister is represented`)
